        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Start with the question, not the kit. For lead in an older home, buy the Tap Score Lead & Copper lab test and take a first-draw sample. For a private well or a first-ever baseline, the Tap Score Advanced panel covers the contaminants that drive treatment choices, and the Watersafe WS-425W is a good annual screen for bacteria and nitrate in between. The Safe Home ULTIMATE is for wells and homes with a specific industrial or agricultural risk.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Keep strips and a TDS meter for what they do well: hardness, chlorine, pH and checking that the filter you bought is still working. They are maintenance tools. The health questions belong to a certified lab, and the answer it gives you is what tells you which filter to buy, or that you do not need one.
